    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** standing as the clear anchor of the offense; his 82.37 efficiency score against Elder is driven by a prime #2 spot and a significant SP Skill advantage (+10%), making him our most essential start for stolen base production. Supporting him are two high-upside plays against the struggling Bradford: **Max Muncy** (68.95) and **Henry Bolte** (65.39). Both benefit from massive park and pitcher-skill adjustments totaling nearly 30% in cumulative positive leverage, allowing **Henry Bolte** to maximize his leadoff position. While **Mickey Moniak** (63.15) faces a tougher arm in Tidwell, his dynamic platoon edge (+14%) justifies his spot in the lineup, providing necessary stability while we look to capitalize on favorable matchups for the rest of the bottom half of the order.\n\nOur most difficult decision of the day involved the marginal 40.43 score for **Zach McKinstry** versus the 39.32 mark for **Jose Caballero**. While **Jose Caballero** remains a high-priority asset due to his elite sprint speed and base-stealing ceiling, the daunting 2.95 xERA of Cease suppressed his efficiency below our 40.0 \"Zebra\" floor, leaving him on the bench. We are proceeding cautiously with **Josh Naylor**, **Cole Young**, and **Isaac Paredes**, as their lineup spots are currently pending; should these lineups shift downward significantly, their efficiency scores\u2014particularly for **Isaac Paredes** against the tough Bryan Woo\u2014could fluctuate. With **James Wood**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, and **Vinnie Pasquantino** all sidelined on the IL, our depth is thinner than we would prefer, placing extra pressure on **Travis Bazzana** and **Austin Riley** to outperform their sub-50 projections if we are to remain competitive in the counting categories tonight.",
